<title>MEXICO: Mexico April manufacturing employment up 5.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Mexico April manufacturing employment up 5.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Employment in Mexico's manufacturing sector rose an average 5.7 percent during April compared with the same month a year ago, the National Statistics Institute (INEGI) said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>The index of hours worked in April rose by an average 13.6 percent year over year, the institute said.</p>
<p>Every manufacturing sector showed a rise in employment, led by machinery and equipment, textiles and wood products.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
</text>
